In summary, excessive phosphorus intake can lead to imbalances in mineral balance, particularly in calcium and magnesium, and can cause kidney damage, impaired bone health, and other health risks. Maintaining a well balance dietary intake of phosphorus and other minerals is essential for optimal health.
