What is the most common cause of hypoparathyroidism?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The most common cause of hypoparathyroidism is the **underruption of the parathyroid glands** during or due to surgery. This occurs because the parathyroid glands are small and located near the thyroid gland, and during thyroid cancer or other thyroid gland symptoms, the glands may be removed or removed in part. This loss of parathyroid tissue reduces the production of parathyroid hormone (PTH), leading to hypoparroidcemic symptoms. $\boxed{\text{The thyroid gland is not closely related to the parathyroid glands.}}$

