1. SH2 and SH3 domains: These small regions on proteins bind to specific amino acid sequences in other proteins, enabling the formation of signaling complexes. In excitotoxicity, dysregulated calcium signaling disrupts cellular homeostasis, leading to neuronal death. By targeting SH2 and SH3 domains, researchers can modulate the activity of proteins involved in calcium signaling pathways, such as Ras-like guanyanine nucleotide-binding factor (GRFI) and mit kinase B (MEK), thereby attenuating excitotoxicity.

