In summary, protein-binding domains can be targeted to modulate the activity of proteins involved in excitotoxicity, thereby treating neurological disorders. This can be achieved by targeting SH2 and SH3 domains to regulate calcium signaling pathways or ligand-binding domains to modulate neurotransmitter receptor activity.
