<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Calculate the equivalents of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) in the 10.0 L of 2.00 N H\(_2\)SO\(_4\):**
   \[
   \text{Equivalents} = \text{Normality} \times \text{Volume (L)} = 2.00 \, \text{N} \times 10.0 \, \text{L} = 20.0 \, \text{eq}
   \]
2. **Determine the equivalents of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) needed in the final solution:**
   \[
   \text{Equivalents} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Volume (L)} = 3.00 \, \text{M} \times 20.0 \, \text{L} = 60.0 \, \text{eq}
   \]
3. **Calculate the difference in equivalents:**
   \[
   \text{Excess equivalents} = 60.0 \, \text{eq} - 20.0 \, \text{eq} = 40.0 \, \text{eq}
   \]
   This means 40.0 equivalents of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) are needed from the 6.00 M solution.

4. **Calculate the volume of 6.00 M H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) required:**
   \[
   \text{Volume (L)} = \frac{\text{Equivalents}}{\text{Molarity}} = \frac{40.0 \, \text{eq}}{6.00 \, \text{M}} = 6.67 \, \text{L}
   \]
   The required volume is \(\boxed{6.67 \, \text{L}}\).
