","(a) The integral of \( 2^x \) is \( \frac{2^x}{\ln 2} \). Evaluating from \(-1\) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{-1}^{1} 2^{x} d x = \left. \frac{2^x}{\ln 2} \right]_{-1}^{1} = \frac{2^1}{\ln 2} - \frac{2^{-1}}{\ln 2} = \frac{2 - \frac{1}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{\frac{3}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{3}{2\ln 2}
\]
(b) The integral of \( 3e^x \) is \( 3e^x \), and the integral of \( 2\sqrt{x} = 2x^{1/2} \) is \( \frac{4}{3}x^{3/2} \). Evaluating from \( 0 \) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+ 2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = \left[ 3e^x + \frac{4}{3}x^{3/2} \right] \Bigg|_{0}^{1} = 3e^1 + \frac{4}{3}1^{3/2} - 3e^0 - \frac{4}{3}0^{3/2} = 3e + \frac{4}{3} - 3 - 0 = 3e - \frac{3}{3} = 3e - 1
\]
(c) The integral of \( 2^{2y} \) is \( \frac{2^{2y}}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{2^{2y}}{2 \ln 2} \). Evaluating from \( 0 \) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y = \left[ \frac{2^{2y}}{2 \ln 2} \right] \Bigg|_{0}^{1} = \frac{2^{2 \cdot 1}}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{2^{2 \cdot 0}}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{4}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{1}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{3}{2 \ln 2}
\]

Final answers:
(a) \( \boxed{\dfrac{3}{2\ln 2}} \)  
(b) \( \boxed{3e - 1} \)  
(c) \( \boxed{\dfrac{3}{2 \ln 2}} \)
