   - The air velocity at the outer edge of the conical duct is \( v_1 = \frac{m_1}{\rho A_1} \), where \( m_1 \) is the mass flow rate, \( \rho \) is the density of air at 20°C (1.226 kg/m³), and \( A_1 \) is the cross-sectional area at the outer edge of the conical duct.
   - The air velocity at the inner edge of the conical duct is \( v_2 = \frac{m_1}{\rho A_2} \), where \( A_2 \) is the cross-sectional area at the inner edge of the conical duct.
