1. **Entropy change of the water**:
   The water absorbs heat at a constant temperature of 220°C (493 K). The entropy increase of the water is:
   \[
   \Delta S_{\text{water}} = \frac{\text{Latent heat absorbed}}{T} = \frac{1858.5}{493} = 3.77 \text{ kJ/kg-K}.
   \]

2. **Entropy change of the gas**:
