1. **Calculate the uncertainty in energy:**
   \[
   \Delta E \times \Delta t \geq h
   \]
   \[
   \Delta E \geq \frac{h}{\Delta t} = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J·s}}{2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 3.313 \times 10^{-11} \text{ J}
   \]
   Convert this to MeV:
   \[
   \Delta E = 3.313 \times 10^{-11} \text{ J} \times \frac{1 \text{ MeV}}{1.602 \times 10^{-13} \text{ J}} = 33.5 \text{ MeV}
   \]

2. **Determine the range of outcomes:**
   The rest energy of the Σ⁺ is 1385 MeV, and the uncertainty in its energy is 33.5 MeV. Therefore, the typical range of outcomes of measurements of its rest energy would be:
   \[
   1385 \text{ MeV} - 33.5 \text{ MeV} \leq E \leq 1385 \text{ MeV} + 33.5 \text{ MeV}
   \]
   \[
   1351.5 \text{ MeV} \leq E \leq 1418.5 \text{ MeV}
   \]

3. **Conclusion:**
   The typical range of outcomes of measurements of the Σ⁺ rest energy is \(\boxed{1351.5 \text{ MeV} \leq E \leq 1418.5 \text{ MeV}}\).
